ate. Probably 4 = solves an identified problem that is directly related to the stated problem (do X to get Y, and Y is part of stated problem). Yes.\n\nEvidence: The tool directly addresses the need to know which R&D projects must comply with Article 12 record-keeping.\n\nParadigm_relatedness (1-4): degree to which idea preserves or modifies paradigm. Options: 4 paradigm breaking introduces new elements AND changes relationship between lab's R&D and compliance obligations, or addresses larger problem of what lab researches. 3 paradigm stretching: changes that relationship (e.g., logging woven into science, new partners...). 2 slightly paradigm stretching: introduces new elements (tools, formats, processes) but still treats compliance as logging practice. 1 paradigm preserving.\n\nThis is internal decision-support tool, questionnaire mapping features to Act. Introduces new element tool but still treats compliance as logging practice. Slightly paradigm stretching? Probably 2 = introduces new elements but still treats compliance as logging practice. Not changing relationship fundamentally. Could be 2.\n\nOriginality (1-4): degree to which idea is not only rare but also ingenious... 4 not expressed before AND ingenious... 3 unusual interesting shows some imagination. 2 interesting. 1 common mundane boring.\n\nClassification audit tool for Annex III is fairly common compliance practice. Common, mundane. Score 1? Maybe 2 interesting? I'd say common. Many labs do classification. So 1 = common, mundane, boring.\n\nAcceptability (1-4): degree to which idea is socially legally politically acceptable. 4 common strategies that violate no norms. This is internal audit tool. Acceptable. Score 4.\n\nImplementability (1-4): degree to which idea can be easily implemented. Some changes, reasonably feasible measures? Build diagnostic questionnaire with legal and technical leads. That's some changes or reasonably feasible. Could be 3 = some changes, or reasonably feasible measures. Not