y default. Might be partial. Effectiveness 3 = reasonable and will contribute to solution (partial). Could be 4? It says prevents developers manually implement logging for every new prototype, maintains prototyping speed while ensuring technical viability for regulatory compliance. Might claim solve. But Article 12 requires more specifics. I'd say 3.\n\nImplementability (1-4): easy to implement at low cost... \nDevelop a Python decorator/middleware layer. Some changes reasonably feasible. So 3 = some changes, or reasonably feasible measures. Could be 4 = easy to implement at low cost? Developing library may be moderate. Probably 3.\n\nAcceptability (1-4): socially legally politically acceptable.\nCommon strategies that violate no norms. Logging inputs may raise privacy concerns but still acceptable. 4 = common strategies that violate no norms or sensibilities. Might be 3? Recording inputs to secure database is standard. Acceptable. I'll give 4.\n\nNeed output format: echo id exactly. For each subscale give <subscale>_evidence sentence then <subscale> integer.\n\nProbably JSON? The instruction says return rating... For each subscale give ... Probably just list lines.\n\nI'll output:\n\nid: P2548\nparadigm_relatedness_evidence: ...\nparadigm_relatedness: 2\netc.\n\nLet's produce clear format.\n\n",
