ed. So 4.\n\nAcceptability: degree to which idea socially legally politically acceptable. 4 = common strategies that violate no norms. Logging middleware is acceptable. Secure immutable storage. Probably 4.\n\nImplementability: degree to which can be easily implemented. 4 = easy low cost or non-radical changes. 3 = some changes reasonably feasible. Developing central software library integrated into pipelines, writing to secure immutable storage. That's significant change? Might be some changes reasonably feasible. Could be 3. Not trivial. Requires engineering effort across all projects. Probably not easy low cost. I'd say 3 = some changes, or reasonably feasible measures.\n\nNeed evidence sentence first then score.\n\nProvide output JSON? Instructions: Return rating echoing its id exactly. For each subscale give \"<subscale>_evidence\" (one sentence) first and then \"<subscale>\" (integer). Probably produce list.\n\nLet's format:\n\nid: P2729\nparadigm_relatedness_evidence: ...\nparadigm_relatedness: 2\n...\n\nMake sure one sentence evidence.\n\nProceed.\n\n",
